{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The relevant information for this reason includes the maximum and minimum outcomes of each lottery. Lottery A has a maximum outcome of 3000 Euros and a minimum outcome of 0 Euros. Lottery B has a maximum outcome of 6000 Euros and a minimum outcome of 0 Euros. The maximum outcomes differ, with B having a higher maximum than A. Since the reason prioritizes the lottery with the more favorable (higher) maximum outcome, and if equal then the more favorable minimum, the reason would prefer Lottery B due to its higher maximum outcome (6000 > 3000). The minimum outcomes are identical (0 Euros), so the tie-breaking condition does not come into play. Thus, the decision reason would clearly prefer Lottery B.",
