  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on comparing maximum outcomes, and if those are equal, then minimum outcomes. In this case, the maximum outcome of Lottery B (6000) is higher than that of Lottery A (3000), so the reason would prefer B. The individual explicitly refers to the higher payout (Auszahlung) as a key factor in their decision, which corresponds directly to the maximum outcome. Although the individual also mentions uncertainty, their justification centers on favoring the higher possible payout, which aligns with the core rule of the decision reason. The fact that both lotteries have the same minimum (0) and no losses makes the minimum outcome irrelevant in both the reason and the report. The individual’s focus on the higher payout as a positive feature matches the decision reason’s preference for the more favorable maximum outcome. Therefore, the information considered (maximum outcome) and the justification (preference for higher payout) align closely with the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 95
}

{
